var DESC_SC={'Speed Bench Press':'Explosive bench press at 50-60% 1RM. Lower controlled, then press up as fast as possible. Reset between each rep \u2014 speed and power are the priority, not grinding.',
'Sled Push':'Drive the sled forward with arms extended, staying low with a 45-degree body angle. Short powerful steps, driving through the balls of your feet. Keep your core braced throughout.',
'Hang Power Clean':'Start at the hang position (bar at mid-thigh). Explosively extend hips and shrug, pulling yourself under the bar to catch in a quarter squat. Reset to hang between reps.',
'Face Pulls':'Using a rope attachment at face height, pull toward your face with elbows high and wide. Squeeze shoulder blades together at the end. Excellent for shoulder health and posture.',
'Weighted Dip':'Add weight via belt or dumbbell between feet. Lower until upper arms are parallel to floor, then press up powerfully. Keep slight forward lean for chest emphasis.',
'Weighted Pull-Ups':'Add weight via belt or dumbbell between feet. Full dead hang at bottom, chin over bar at top. Control the descent \u2014 no kipping or swinging.',
'Barbell Thrusters':'Front squat into overhead press in one fluid motion. Squat to depth, then use the momentum from standing to drive the bar overhead. Full lockout at top.',
'AMRAP 5min: 10 KB Swing + 5 Burpees':'As Many Rounds As Possible in 5 minutes. Complete 10 kettlebell swings and 5 burpees, then repeat. Track total rounds completed.',
'EMOM 8min: 5 Thrusters + 10 Mountain Climbers':'Every Minute On the Minute for 8 minutes. Complete 5 thrusters and 10 mountain climbers at the start of each minute. Rest the remainder.',
'EMOM 5min: 3 Burpees + 5 KB Swings':'Every Minute On the Minute for 5 minutes. Complete 3 burpees and 5 kettlebell swings at the start of each minute. Rest the remainder.',
'Tabata Burpees':'8 rounds of 20 seconds max effort burpees, 10 seconds rest. Full Tabata protocol \u2014 push hard during work intervals.',
'Tabata Mountain Climbers':'8 rounds of 20 seconds max effort mountain climbers, 10 seconds rest. Drive knees fast and stay in a strong plank position.',
'Barbell Walking Lunges':'Bar on back in squat position. Step forward into a deep lunge, then drive through front heel to step the back foot forward into the next lunge. Alternate legs continuously.',
'Barbell Hip Thrust':'Sit on floor with upper back against bench, barbell across hips. Drive through heels to lift hips until body forms a straight line from knees to shoulders. Squeeze glutes at top.',
'Barbell Front Squat':'Bar racked on front delts with elbows high. Squat to depth keeping torso upright. Requires good thoracic mobility and core bracing.',
'Barbell Close-Grip Bench Press':'Hands shoulder-width or slightly narrower. Lower bar to lower chest, then press up. Emphasizes triceps more than standard bench.',
'Barbell Curl':'Stand with barbell, arms extended. Curl the weight up by flexing elbows, keeping upper arms stationary. Control the descent \u2014 no swinging.',
'Kettlebell Clean & Press':'Swing the bell between legs, then clean it to rack position in one motion. From the rack, press overhead to full lockout. Lower back to rack, then swing down. One fluid movement.',
'Kettlebell Snatch':'One explosive movement from between the legs to overhead lockout. The bell should travel close to the body and punch through at the top \u2014 not loop wide.',
'Kettlebell Turkish Get-Up':'From lying flat, press KB overhead and methodically stand up through a series of transitions while keeping the weight locked out overhead. Reverse to return. Builds total-body stability.',
'Dumbbell Rear Delt Flyes':'Bent at hips 45-60 degrees, arms hanging. Raise dumbbells out to sides with slight elbow bend, squeezing rear delts. Control the descent.',
'Dumbbell Incline Press':'On incline bench (30-45 degrees), press dumbbells from chest level to full lockout overhead. Targets upper chest and front delts.',
'Dumbbell Renegade Row':'In push-up position with hands on dumbbells. Row one dumbbell to hip while stabilizing with the other arm. Alternate sides. Demands core stability.',
'Personal Best Flow':'Free movement session \u2014 do whatever feels good. Celebrate your progress and enjoy moving your body. Dance, stretch, play.',
'Light Bench/Squat/Swings':'Light, easy versions of your main lifts at 50-60% normal weight. Focus on movement quality and blood flow, not intensity. This is active recovery.',
'Gentle Stretch':'Easy, relaxed stretching. Hold each position 30-60 seconds. No forcing \u2014 breathe into each stretch. Focus on areas that feel tight.',
'Fun partner/solo WOD':'Create your own workout of the day! Pick 3-5 movements you enjoy and set a time cap. The goal is to have fun and move.'};
